  "body": "The prepared class-balanced conditions experiment now has an actual 32-update run, frozen outputs, and an independent recount. It recovered two of four N11-added false negatives, but training exact IR remained 153/168 versus N11's 154/168, so it failed the acceptance rule and is not promoted.\n\nArchive the reviewed recipes and public evidence, including the complete 40-file source inventory and the verified [comparison weights](https://huggingface.co/Publicus/legal-ir-autoencoder/tree/77e33d1c07b09a421b272e3ccb0af229933a7f82/releases/20261014-conditions-balanced-v1). Preserve the incoming source-alignment, ingestion, scheduler, and gitlink changes. Genuine latent decoding, statutory fidelity, broader logic families, isolated numerical reload, and Lean compilation remain unqualified.\n\nValidation: all 62 outputs qualified and frozen; analyzer and independent recount agree; all 176 Hub files pass immutable byte readback and all 5,269 prior identities are preserved. The Git change contains only 141 added report/evidence paths and passes `git diff --check`.\n\nHosted CodeQL checks did not start because the account is locked by a billing issue. Queued self-hosted jobs are not claimed as passes.\n",
  "changed_files": 141,
